{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1779312198,"nonce":"w+hQAz/QFzHC4Im7vMxlgRs/uZE=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABCx0Hvs68z4AN"},"target":"93c2144bcd7a717be0191e20aeb26c73e9d2df8d4cbf7b1c72ea7eb43b9b2341","message":"## Background\n\nDuring [#135 deployment (2026-05-19)](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135) Phase 1, the nav stack failed to bring up mid-deployment:\n\n```\nlocal_costmap: Timed out waiting for transform from bizzy/base_link to bizzy/map_tide ... frame does not exist\nlifecycle_manager_navigation: Failed to bring up all requested nodes. Aborting bringup.\nbt_task_navigator: Action server is inactive. Rejecting the goal.\n```\n\n## Root cause (confirmed in-field — see gabby log §13)\n\n`sea_surface_estimator` was suppressing every tide estimate as implausible — observed estimate was ~`−12.8 m`, while the chart-datum plausibility band was `[−33.74, −19.42]`. With all estimates rejected, no `map → map_tide` transform was ever broadcast, cascading through `local_costmap` → `controller_server` → action-server activation failure.\n\nSnapshot of altitudes during the failure:\n\n| Source | Altitude | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos` | +8.11 m (MSL) | with `undulation: -32.49 m`; ellipsoidal ≈ -24.38 m |\n| `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/ekf_nav` | +7.19 m (MSL) | with `undulation: -32.49 m`; ellipsoidal ≈ -25.30 m |\n| `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/global` | **-12.39 m** | (no undulation; EKF-fused) |\n| `/bizzy/tide_estimate` | **-12.44 m** | tracks mavros, not SBG |\n\n`/bizzy/tide_estimate` was tracking mavros `/global` (EKF-fused, referenced to EKF origin / home), **not** the ellipsoidal SBG MSL+undulation that the chart-datum band expects. Geoid undulation at this latitude is ~25 m; the mavros `/global` Z lands ~13 m above the plausible chart-datum band.\n\n## Triggering change\n\nCommit `e604a36e` (2026-04-28, `unh_echoboats_project11`) switched both `mru_transform` topic mappings in `config/bizzyboat.yaml` (lines 25 + 43):\n\n```diff\n-            position: \"mavros/global_position/raw/fix\"\n-            velocity: \"mavros/global_position/raw/gps_vel\"\n+            position: \"mavros/global_position/global\"\n+            velocity: \"mavros/local_position/velocity_body\"\n```\n\n`mavros/global_position/global` is ArduPilot's EKF-fused position; downstream `/bizzy/odom` therefore had a Z ~13 m above where chart-datum-aligned code expects the sea surface to be.\n\n## Field workaround (current state)\n\nField commit `c36acfa` (2026-05-19, on `gitcloud:field/unh_echoboats_project11` `jazzy`; cherry-picked onto PR #136 as `ece31dc`) reverted both lines back to `raw/fix` / `raw/gps_vel`. Mission completed on this workaround.\n\nPost-revert verification (gabby log §13):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `bizzy/base_link` → `bizzy/map_tide` TF | ✓ resolved, Z = −0.078 m (boat 7.8 cm below sea surface — sane) |\n| `/bizzy/tide_estimate` | ✓ −23.77 m (inside plausible band) |\n| `sea_surface_estimator` suppression warnings (new log) | ✓ 0 |\n| Nav lifecycle (controller_server etc.) | ✓ all active |\n\n## Durable options\n\nThe revert is mission-enabling but not necessarily the right long-term choice. Three options to weigh:\n\n### A. Keep the revert: `mavros/global_position/raw/fix`\n\n- ✅ Restores pre-04-28 behavior; immediately works\n- ❌ Loses whatever the 04-28 switch was for (`raw/fix` may have less-clean velocity, no EKF benefits)\n- Cost: zero (already in place)\n\n### B. Switch to SBG: `sensors/sbg/gps_pos` (or `…/ekf_nav`)\n\n- ✅ Chart_datum is SBG-aligned (MLLW grids); puts the altitude in a coherent frame\n- ✅ Higher-quality nav data than raw GPS\n- ⚠️ **SBG is a temporary class-loaner** (returning after the June 2026 hydro class — see workspace memory `project_bizzyboat_sbg_temporary`). Hard-depending on `sbg_driver` is what that memory specifically warns against.\n- ❓ Needs message-type compat check (`mru_transform` expects what type?)\n- Cost: yaml swap + verification\n\n### C. Keep mavros `/global` with geoid compensation\n\n- ✅ Keeps EKF benefits\n- ✅ Doesn't depend on SBG\n- ❌ Most complex: need to compute ellipsoidal from EKF Z + known geoid undulation. EKF-origin / home semantics get involved.\n- Cost: real code change\n\n## Related work\n\n- `0507eda` (git-bug, no GitHub counterpart yet) — *nav: define lever-arm/base_link contract for SBG and mavros position streams*\n- `57a6134` (git-bug, no GitHub counterpart yet) — *urdf: model SBG INS, GNSS antenna(s), and IMU mounting alignment on bizzyboat*\n\nBoth are upstream of the nav-input choice — settling the lever-arm/base_link contract clarifies what frame each source actually publishes in. May be worth resolving those first.\n\n## Suggested next step\n\nDecide A vs B vs C with input from the upstream URDF/lever-arm work. Add a regression test on `sea_surface_estimator` plausibility-band agreement with the chosen source's altitude frame so this can't silently break again the next time a nav-input swap is considered.\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`\n\n---\n\n## Update 2026-05-20: chosen direction — FCU reconfiguration (subsumes #111 mavros side)\n\nAfter cross-deployment review, the durable answer is **Option C, in the form of an FCU-side reconfiguration** rather than a bridge-side geoid compensation. One coordinated set of FCU parameter changes delivers both the durable Z-reference choice (this issue) AND the outstanding mavros half of [#111](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111) lever-arm contract:\n\n| Param | Value | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `EK3_SRC1_POSZ` | `3` (GPS) | FCU EKF Z stops tracking baro / weather pressure; tracks GPS altitude instead. Closes the Z-reference question. |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_X` / `_Y` / `_Z` | per-boat | Tell EKF where the GPS antenna is relative to the EKF origin / `base_link` so the EKF reports at `base_link`. |\n| `GPS_POS1_X` / `_Y` / `_Z` | per-boat | Tell ArduPilot the primary GPS antenna's physical offset. Required pair for the EKF offset above to be applied correctly. |\n\n**Rationale for FCU reconfig vs in-bridge compensation:**\n\n- Compensation in a bridge node adds latency, an extra topic, and a third place (after URDF + sbgCenter + ArduPilot) where lever-arm config can drift.\n- The FCU already does GPS lever-arm and Z-source selection natively. Using those parameters keeps the configuration auditable on the boat itself and matches the convention #111 documents for the SBG side (sbgCenter Output Location).\n\n**What this subsumes from [#111](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111):**\n\n- #111's SBG half was resolved live 2026-05-01 via sbgCenter Output Location.\n- #111's mavros half — making `mavros/global_position/*` report at `base_link` — is exactly what `EK3_GPS_OFFS` + `GPS_POS1_*` accomplish. No separate work item required.\n\nPlan: close #111 with a pointer here once this lands. Track #110 (URDF gap) separately — it's documentation-correctness and doesn't gate this reconfig.\n\n**Validation:**\n\n- Bench check the parameter changes against a known antenna-offset value (whatever values come out of #77's offset measurements).\n- At least one deployment to confirm both that (a) baro-related Z drift is gone, and (b) `mavros/global_position/*` reports at `base_link` (body-frame SBG − MAV offset drops to GPS-CEP territory, not the 0.64 m steady offset documented in #111).\n- Add a regression test on `sea_surface_estimator` plausibility-band agreement with the chosen source's altitude frame so the next nav-input swap can't silently re-break this.\n\n**Timeline:** Must finish before 2026-06-04 — Summer Hydro 2026 class start. Lake Massabesic survey 2026-06-15.","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779228564,"nonce":"i+vhbNFnj9BRLkpbVUHZBHdEGXw=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABCx0Hvs8AAAAF_ZVf1Q"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779245837,"nonce":"4eFUHl1ad3FiCh50BxwDNPhHN7I=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABC95d2g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4494089690"},"message":"## 2026-05-19 post-mission analysis: rules out Option C (mavros `/global` + geoid compensation)\n\nBag analysis of the 2026-05-19 boat-side bag adds a finding that wasn't visible from the in-field snapshots: `mavros/global_position/global` doesn't just have a *frame-reference* problem (EKF origin / home vs ellipsoidal), it has a **monotonic upward Z drift of ~5 m/hour**. Per-minute altitude across sources during today's deployment:\n\n| EDT | mav_raw_alt | mav_global_alt | bizzy_odom_z | sbg+undulation (ellipsoidal) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 12:10 | -21.05 | -21.41 | -21.41 | -21.56 |\n| 12:30 | -24.11 | -21.63 | -21.63 | -24.68 |\n| 13:00 | -23.93 | -14.27 | -14.27 | -24.46 |\n| 13:10 | -23.89 | -12.78 | -12.78 | -24.46 |\n| 13:30 | -23.78 | -11.51 | **-23.78** | -24.36 |\n| 13:45 | -23.76 | -9.44 | -23.82 | -24.32 |\n| 14:00 | -23.79 | -6.40 | -23.79 | -24.36 |\n\n`mavros/global_position/global` drifts monotonically from −21 m → −2.5 m (~18.5 m climb over ~2 h ≈ **5 m/h**, no apparent leveling). With the boat on calm water — no vertical motion — this is the EKF freely drifting in Z because nothing constrains it. Likely missing GPS altitude updates feeding the EKF.\n\n`/bizzy/odom` pos_z jumps cleanly from −11.51 m → −23.78 m at 13:30 EDT — exact moment of the revert + full-stack relaunch. Post-revert `/bizzy/odom` tracks `mavros/raw/fix` within \u003c 0.1 m and stays stable while `/global` keeps drifting.\n\n### Implication for Option C\n\nThe original gabby log §13 framing offered three durable options:\n\n- A: revert to `mavros/global_position/raw/fix` (the field workaround)\n- B: switch to SBG (`gps_pos` or `ekf_nav`)\n- C: keep `mavros/global` with geoid compensation\n\nToday's drift evidence **rules out Option C**. Even with perfect geoid compensation, the underlying Z would still drift +5 m/h and `sea_surface_estimator`'s plausibility check would reject estimates within ~2 hours. Option C would only buy time, not fix the problem.\n\nSo the real choice is A vs B:\n\n- **A (mavros raw/fix)** — already in place. SBG ellipsoidal (altitude + undulation) agrees with mavros raw/fix within ~0.4 m today, so both are usable as nav inputs. Concerns: (a) the previous-deployment-related question of \"do these report at `base_link` or at the GNSS antenna\" still applies — see [`#110`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/110) / [`#111`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111); (b) what was the 2026-04-28 commit `e604a36e` actually trying to achieve by switching to `/global`?\n- **B (SBG)** — clean now while the loaner Ellipse-D is on board; depends on SBG being present (per memory `project_bizzyboat_sbg_temporary` it's going back after the June 2026 class). Hard-coding SBG dependence would force a re-revert when the SBG leaves.\n\n### Velocity is fine across all sources\n\nMavros `local_position/odom` velocity and SBG `ekf_nav` velocity agree within ~10 mm/s throughout the deployment (0.2–0.4 m/s drift, 1.5–1.7 m/s under mission speed). The drift problem is **altitude-specific to the EKF path** — velocity-side fusion is healthy. Doesn't change the A vs B choice but reassures that whichever source feeds attitude/velocity is fine.\n\n### Source\n\nBoat-side bag SQLite at `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-19/bizzyboat.db`. Query for the altitude table above is in the dev log's \"Post-mission data review\" section of [PR #136](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/136).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779253542,"nonce":"w8HzhncQ56x1kp3N4ZXQL3nUSeE=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABC-eYvg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4494694590"},"message":"## Update: Option C is back on the table\n\nFollowing the [earlier post-mission comment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4494089690) that ruled out Option C (mavros `/global` + geoid compensation) based on the Z drift, a follow-up investigation found the **root cause is fixable via a single FCU param change**.\n\n### Hypothesis: the EKF Z drift is tracking atmospheric pressure\n\nCube Orange has the MS5611 barometer. If the EKF uses baro as its primary vertical position source, EKF Z follows local atmospheric pressure — which drifts with weather, not with the boat's actual altitude.\n\n### Weather evidence supports it\n\nMETAR for KPSM (Pease, ~20 km from the deployment site) during the on-water window:\n\n| EDT | SLP (hPa) | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| 12:55 | 1012.4 | early deployment |\n| 13:55 | 1011.4 | mid |\n| 14:55 | 1011.0 | post-recovery |\n| 15:55 | 1010.0 | **−TSRA (thunderstorm)** |\n\nPressure dropped 1.4 hPa over the 2-hour deployment window. At 8.5 m/hPa, that predicts ~12 m of apparent altitude increase. The bag showed ~15 m of EKF Z drift over ~1.5 hours. Same direction, same order of magnitude, with a thunderstorm hitting shortly after recovery — the classic falling-pressure-ahead-of-storm pattern.\n\n### Smoking gun in the FCU params\n\nFrom `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_baseline.param`:\n\n```\nEK3_SRC1_POSXY   3        # GPS for horizontal position\nEK3_SRC1_POSZ    1        # *** Baro for vertical position ***\nEK3_SRC1_VELXY   3        # GPS for horizontal velocity\nEK3_SRC1_VELZ    3        # GPS for vertical velocity\n```\n\nArduPilot's `EK3_SRCx_POSZ` values: 1 = Baro, 3 = GPS. **The EKF's primary vertical position source is the barometer.** That's the ArduRover default — sensible for ground vehicles where GPS altitude is unreliable. For a marine vehicle on water with RTK GPS, it's wrong, and explains today's drift exactly.\n\nAlso slightly inconsistent: `EK3_SRC1_VELZ` is already 3 (GPS), so the FCU trusts GPS for vertical *velocity* but not vertical *position*.\n\n### Option C revised — recommended durable answer\n\nThe original motivation for the 2026-04-28 switch to `mavros/global_position/global` (commit `e604a36e`) was right:\n\n- **base_link reference frame** (vs. raw/fix which is at the GPS antenna — relates to `#110`/`#111` lever-arm work)\n- **EKF fusion benefits** (IMU smoothing, multi-sensor)\n\nOption A (revert to `raw/fix`) is the current workaround but loses both benefits. The durable answer is:\n\n1. **Change `EK3_SRC1_POSZ` from 1 (baro) to 3 (GPS)** on the BizzyBoat FCU\n2. Validate post-change behavior on a static test — confirm EKF Z stays stable across weather pressure changes\n3. **Restore the 2026-04-28 `mavros/global_position/global` switch** in `bizzyboat.yaml`\n4. Close this issue\n\nFor consistency, also set `EK3_SRC2_POSZ` and `EK3_SRC3_POSZ` to 3 (they're currently 1 but the SRC2/SRC3 source sets aren't otherwise configured — currently inactive).\n\n### Enabling sub-tasks (worth doing alongside)\n\n- **`/bizzy/mavros/imu/static_pressure`** — bag this so future deployments can verify pressure-tracking quantitatively against METAR. Add to `bizzyboat.yaml` recording.\n- **Enable the mavros `altitude` plugin.** Currently in the workspace `apm_pluginlists.yaml` `denylist`, so `/mavros/altitude` doesn't exist on BizzyBoat at all. Enabling it gives us amsl / local / relative / terrain altitude side-by-side in one topic — a much richer altitude-source surface for any future debugging. Add `/bizzy/mavros/altitude` to bag list once enabled.\n- **`/bizzy/mavros/global_position/rel_alt`** — altitude relative to home (boat-local).\n\n### Other params worth a second look once `EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 3` is in\n\n- `EK3_GPS_VACC_MAX = 0.000000` — vertical accuracy check disabled. With RTK active it's fine; without RTK you'd want a threshold to reject degraded GPS altitudes\n- `EK3_ALT_M_NSE = 2.0` — altitude measurement noise. With GPS-altitude (RTK ~10 cm), this is generous; could be tightened for sharper EKF response\n\n### Source\n\nAnalysis in [PR #136](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/136) dev log \"Post-mission data review\" §5 and §6 (METAR data + EK3 param table).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779372068,"nonce":"9ICrY62MVz/r03y3QtHTUcPINrM=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDMILOA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138#issuecomment-4509010744"},"message":"## Update 2026-05-21: primary nav source clarification + concrete param diff\n\nSurfacing two clarifications and the exact 4-param diff so a field-side\nagent reading this via git-bug has everything needed without cross-issue\nlookups.\n\n### Primary nav source: CUAV-on-Cube, not SBG\n\nThe 2026-05-20 Update above leaves ambiguous which GPS the `EK3_GPS_OFFS`\nand `GPS_POS1_*` values are for. The answer: the **CUAV C-RTK 2HP\nconnected to the Cube Orange** is the primary navigation GPS. The SBG\nEllipse-D is **payload-only** (sonar / hydro pipeline) — available in\nROS as monitoring or backup, but not the primary nav input that\nArduPilot sees.\n\nThat fixes the offset numbers in the FCU params to the CUAV antenna\npose (see `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_reference_geometry.md`\n§\"2x CUAV C-RTK 2HP GNSS Antennas\" and `bizzyboat_offsets.svg`).\n\n### Concrete 4-param diff (verified against current FCU param files)\n\nVerified against `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param`\n(applied) and `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_baseline.param`\n(defaults):\n\n| Param | Currently on boat | Target | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `EK3_SRC1_POSZ` | `1` (baro) | `3` (GPS) | Stops EKF Z tracking atmospheric pressure |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_X` | (unset → 0) | `0.835` | CUAV forward antenna X (m), ahead of `base_link` |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_Y` | (unset → 0) | `0.000` | Centerline |\n| `EK3_GPS_OFFS_Z` | (unset → 0) | `-0.890` | CUAV antenna 0.89 m above `base_link` (ArduPilot: negative = up) |\n| `GPS_POS1_X / Y / Z` | `0.835 / 0.000 / -0.890` | unchanged | Already correct from #91 — do not touch |\n\nOnly the four EK3 rows change today. `GPS_POS1_*` is already set\ncorrectly from the earlier #91 work; touching it would risk regressing it.\n\n### Application mechanism\n\nRoland applies the 4 changes interactively via MAVProxy at the dock,\nwith the gabby-side agent guiding. Sequence:\n\n```text\nparam set EK3_SRC1_POSZ 3\nparam set EK3_GPS_OFFS_X 0.835\nparam set EK3_GPS_OFFS_Y 0.0\nparam set EK3_GPS_OFFS_Z -0.89\nparam save                       # persist to FCU\n# then reboot the Cube; wait for EKF home set + GPS lock\nparam show EK3_SRC1_POSZ EK3_GPS_OFFS_X EK3_GPS_OFFS_Y EK3_GPS_OFFS_Z\n```\n\nQGC file-load is not used; no `.parm` artifact in this PR.\n\n### Validation (covered in [#149 day plan](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149) Block 2)\n\n- `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/mavros/global_position/global -n 1` → Z plausibly\n  in the SBG MSL+undulation chart-datum range (not the previous ~−12 m).\n- `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/tide_estimate -n 1` → inside plausibility band,\n  no `sea_surface_estimator` suppression warnings.\n- Mission-scale: body-frame SBG − MAV offset should drop toward GPS-CEP\n  (sub-decimeter ideally), not the 0.64 m steady offset documented in #111.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}